>>
Rule 13 (If dtype is complex128, then start and end can be float or complex tensors)
{v_1 : dtype, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 10 then (dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10) ∧ (dtype_(v_3) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_3) = 10)
>>
Rule 14 (If out is specified, the dtype should match start and end)
